vv vendors librdata — Evan Miller's reader for R's .rds / .RData files — to
open R data frames. Only the read side is kept:
  rdata_read.c, rdata_parser.c, rdata_bits.c, rdata_error.c,
  rdata_io_unistd.c, CKHashTable.c and their headers.
The writer (rdata_write.c), the examples, tests and fuzzers are dropped.
Compression (gzip / bzip2 / xz) uses zlib, libbz2 and liblzma; strings are
converted with iconv.

Local patches (marked `vv:` in the code):
  rdata_read.c       reset_stream frees strm_buffer before init_stream
                     allocates another (64 KiB leaked per compressed .rds).
  rdata_io_unistd.c,
  rdata_parser.c     the default unistd io context is owned by the parser and
                     freed in rdata_parser_free (rdata_unistd_io_init marked it
                     external, so it was never freed).
  rdata_read.c       read_string_vector_n rejects string lengths below -1
                     (NA) instead of passing (size_t)(len + 1) to realloc;
                     UTF-8 buffer sizes are computed in size_t.
  rdata_read.c       compact sequences (ALTREP, e.g. 1:n) are limited to
                     RDATA_MAX_COMPACT_SEQ elements, 2^27 by default and 2^20
                     in fuzz builds (they are materialized from three
                     numbers, so a few bytes could otherwise ask for 16 GB),
                     integer
                     sequences must stay within int32, and the sequence
                     buffers are checked for NULL.
  rdata_read.c       read_value_vector_data rejects negative lengths; it,
                     read_character_string and read_string_vector_n read
                     through read_st_alloc, which grows the buffer as data
                     arrives instead of allocating the declared length up
                     front.
  rdata_read.c       lseek_st skips compressed data through a fixed 64 KiB
                     buffer instead of allocating the skipped length.
  rdata_read.c       an unnamed dimnames axis (NULL) is reported with one
                     dim_name_handler(NULL, 0) call instead of one call per
                     declared element of that dimension.
  rdata_read.c       integer-backed Date / POSIXct vectors are converted to
                     doubles before the column handler sees them (the handler
                     received int32 data typed as DATE / TIMESTAMP, which
                     callers read as doubles past the end of the buffer).

To bump the pinned version: replace the files above from the new commit and
update this UPSTREAM file.
